  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Addition of alc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KOH</mi></math> to haloalkanes follows the Saytzeff rule which points towards greater stability. Saytzeff&#39;s rule implies that elimination reactions favour formation of alkene with greater number of substituents.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/def9c059-c492-4e0a-8e19-5ed7876d30bf-61f18e57-7060-4a94-a630-0a661010fea7-image.png\" style=\"width: 185px; height: 75px;\" /><br /><br />Not only that, but it also gives the molecule an extended conjugate system which further enhances its stability.</p>",
